  "result": "Perfect! All 155 tests pass. I've successfully added payment terms support:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/errors.js** - Added error code:\n   - TERMS_INVALID - for unknown payment terms\n\n2. **src/invoices.js**:\n   - Updated `createInvoice()` to accept optional `terms` parameter\n   - Defaults to 'NET30' if not specified\n   - Validates terms and calculates `dueDate`:\n     - **NET14**: issueDate + 14 days\n     - **NET30**: issueDate + 30 days (default)\n     - **EOM**: last day of the issue date's month\n   - Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` in returned invoice\n   - Returns TERMS_INVALID error for unknown terms\n   - Uses UTC-aware date calculations via `Date.UTC()`\n\n3. **test/invoices.test.js** - 7 new tests covering:\n   - Default NET30 behavior\n   - NET14 and NET30 day calculations\n   - EOM calculation (month-end)\n   - EOM edge cases (February in non-leap year)\n   - Invalid terms rejection\n\n**Key design**: All date calculations work entirely in UTC using `Date.UTC()` to ensure consistency regardless of the machine's local timezone.",
